## SECTION 0 — Orientation & Non-Negotiable Rules (paste first)

You are building `narrowdown`, a generic, production-grade Python library that reduces LLM
token cost for ANY application calling an OpenAI-compatible OR Gemini-style API. Supports
synchronous chat-completions and asynchronous enqueue/poll.

**Allowed third-party deps — EXACTLY these:** `pydantic` (v2), `pydantic-settings`, `tiktoken`,
`spacy`. Everything else stdlib.

**Hard rules (any violation = build failure):**

- No ML model downloads at runtime. No HuggingFace / transformers / sentence-transformers /
  perplexity / embedding models. No network calls from the library itself.
- MUST import and run with the spaCy model absent (regex fallback for NER).
- No placeholders / TODO / `pass`-only stubs / `NotImplementedError`. Fully implement
  everything; if you cannot, STOP and say so.
- Never mutate caller input; deep-copy.
- **Fail-safe everywhere** (see philosophy): per-stage try/except returning the stage input on
  error; whole-pipeline try/except returning the original request on error; never raise out of
  `optimize()` for processing errors (only raise `NarrowdownError` for clearly invalid input
  shapes, and even then the adapters never crash a call).
- **No budget/ceiling logic at all.** No max-token cap, no turn dropping.
- Compression is revert-not-drop (QualityGate per block).
- `NARROWDOWN_BYPASS=1` is an identity function.
- `shadow=True` returns ORIGINAL messages but a full report.
- Async/queue mode disables features needing a synchronous round trip.
- Thread-safe; per-instance state; no module-level mutable singletons.
- Python 3.10+, Windows + Linux.

