## SECTION 5 — Content Router (fail-safe)

Create `narrowdown/pipeline/router.py` → `class ContentRouter`,
`route(messages)->(list[list[Block]], list[RoutingDecision])`. Priority:

1. SKIP+protected: every `role=="system"`; AND the LAST `role=="user"` message.
1. Split content on fenced code blocks (regex ````(\w+)?\n.*?\n````, DOTALL), order
   preserved for exact reassembly.
1. Classify each non-skip segment: BINARY (utf-8 round-trip fails or base64 blob heuristic
   len>500 & >85% base64 chars); JSON (`json.loads`→dict/list, or fence tag json); CODE (fence
   tag in {py,python,java,js,javascript,ts,typescript,go,rust,cpp,c,cs,rb,php}; or `ast.parse`
   ok; or Java markers `(public|private|protected)\s+(class|interface|void|static)` /
   `@(Override|Service|Repository|Component|Autowired)`); LOG (≥60% non-empty lines match
   `^\s*(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}|\[?(DEBUG|INFO|WARN|WARNING|ERROR|FATAL|TRACE))` or `at [\w.$]+\(` or
   `Traceback (most recent call last)`); else PROSE.

If a single segment classification raises, treat that segment as PROSE (safe default) and log.

**TEST:** system→SKIP/protected; last user→SKIP/protected; JSON→JSON; ````java`→CODE;
bare Python→CODE; timestamped→LOG; paragraph→PROSE; mixed→ordered multi-block; a segment that
triggers a parser error → falls back to PROSE, no exception.
